08, "d": 0.119583, "w": "we"}, {"t": 12.989125, "d": 0.217375, "w": "didn't"}, {"t": 13.217375, "d": 0.119583, "w": "know"}, {"t": 13.347833, "d": 0.076083, "w": "the"}, {"t": 13.434791, "d": 0.489125, "w": "cause"}], "duration": 14.256708333333334, "spoken": "That's different from the original ResNet paper, where deeper plain networks had higher training error. Ours trained fine and fell on validation. Residual connections are the standard fix for deep plain networks, so they were a natural next thing to try, even though we didn't know the cause."}